WEBVTT

1
00:00:15.187 --> 00:00:15.948
Henry called.

2
00:00:15.968 --> 00:00:18.929
"Wait! What are you talking about?"

3
00:00:18.949 --> 00:00:20.750
"Who cares?"

4
00:00:21.070 --> 00:00:21.711
Maggie said.

5
00:00:21.731 --> 00:00:24.372
"We care," Henry said.

6
00:00:24.392 --> 00:00:26.814
"What if Nora took that painting?"

7
00:00:27.854 --> 00:00:28.695
Cole gasped.

8
00:00:28.715 --> 00:00:30.756
"That actually makes sense!

9
00:00:31.636 --> 00:00:34.619
Well, as much sense as anything Nora ever does, anyway.

10
00:00:35.580 --> 00:00:40.064
Nora seemed really upset when she heard Nathan's painting might end up in the museum."

11
00:00:40.084 --> 00:00:43.627
"Exactly," Henry agreed.

12
00:00:43.647 --> 00:00:47.550
"And the stuff she was saying a minute ago made her sound guilty."

13
00:00:47.570 --> 00:00:50.913
"So are we adding her to the suspect list?"

14
00:00:51.274 --> 00:00:51.914
asked Maggie.

15
00:00:51.934 --> 00:00:54.256
"Definitely," Cole said.

16
00:00:54.276 --> 00:00:58.000
"She's sneaky enough to snatch that painting and hide it somewhere."

17
00:00:59.216 --> 00:01:04.419
"Luckily, we already know she's not very good at covering her tracks," Henry said, smiling.

18
00:01:05.480 --> 00:01:10.203
He was talking about an earlier case involving Nora, which had led to her adopting Patches.

19
00:01:10.223 --> 00:01:13.605
"Let's go look for clues at the scene of the crime."

20
00:01:13.625 --> 00:01:17.928
"Okay." Maggie put out the Closed sign again.

21
00:01:17.948 --> 00:01:20.789
"How much time do we have before judging starts?"

22
00:01:22.010 --> 00:01:23.211
Henry glanced at his phone.

23
00:01:23.231 --> 00:01:24.872
"Almost an hour."

24
00:01:28.416 --> 00:01:29.897
They hurried over to the art show.

25
00:01:30.857 --> 00:01:35.459
When they arrived at the empty spot where Nathan's painting had been, Nathan wasn't there.

26
00:01:36.419 --> 00:01:37.660
But someone else was.

27
00:01:37.680 --> 00:01:39.441
"Hi, Mr.

28
00:01:39.461 --> 00:01:40.781
Collins," Henry said.

29
00:01:40.801 --> 00:01:42.342
"What are you doing?"

30
00:01:43.462 --> 00:01:45.884
Mr. Collins spun around and laughed sheepishly.

31
00:01:45.904 --> 00:01:47.824
"Oh! You startled me."

32
00:01:47.844 --> 00:01:50.445
"Were you looking for Nathan's painting?"

33
00:01:50.726 --> 00:01:51.446
Maggie asked.

34
00:01:51.466 --> 00:01:53.307
"Yes, I admit it."

35
00:01:53.927 --> 00:01:56.108
Mr. Collins tugged on his flowered tie.

36
00:01:57.304 --> 00:01:59.765
"It's been on my mind ever since I saw it this morning.

37
00:02:00.886 --> 00:02:04.408
Can you believe two artists found such similar inspiration?

38
00:02:05.469 --> 00:02:07.970
Young Nathan's subject could be the twin of mine!"

39
00:02:07.990 --> 00:02:10.911
"Um, okay."

40
00:02:11.192 --> 00:02:12.372
Cole sounded doubtful.

41
00:02:13.093 --> 00:02:14.693
Henry knew what his friend was thinking.

42
00:02:15.634 --> 00:02:18.776
Mr. Collins' crazy cat painting looked nothing like Nathan's!

43
00:02:18.796 --> 00:02:22.458
"What if the judges think your paintings are too similar?"

44
00:02:22.678 --> 00:02:23.378
Maggie asked.

45
00:02:23.398 --> 00:02:26.660
"Are you worried they might not pick yours for the museum?"

46
00:02:27.736 --> 00:02:28.677
"I suppose not."

47
00:02:29.277 --> 00:02:31.018
Mr. Collins winked and smiled.

48
00:02:31.038 --> 00:02:36.161
"Nathan and I are not even in the same age category, in case you couldn't tell.

49
00:02:37.401 --> 00:02:39.422
I'm just worrying over nothing, as usual!

50
00:02:40.163 --> 00:02:42.164
It's the curse of being a sensitive artist."

51
00:02:43.385 --> 00:02:44.785
He glanced at the empty spot.

52
00:02:44.805 --> 00:02:47.387
"So where is your friend's masterpiece?"

53
00:02:48.607 --> 00:02:50.528
"We're not sure," Henry said.

54
00:02:50.548 --> 00:02:53.510
"It disappeared about forty minutes ago."

55
00:02:53.530 --> 00:02:55.171
"Oh dear!"

56
00:02:55.431 --> 00:02:56.852
Mr. Collins looked alarmed.

57
00:02:57.556 --> 00:02:59.217
"Is there an art thief at the show?"

58
00:02:59.238 --> 00:03:01.720
"Maybe," Cole said.

59
00:03:01.740 --> 00:03:04.001
"Have you seen anything suspicious?"

60
00:03:04.021 --> 00:03:06.864
"Where have you been for the past hour?"

61
00:03:07.904 --> 00:03:09.346
Maggie demanded before Mr.

62
00:03:09.366 --> 00:03:10.467
Collins could respond.

63
00:03:11.527 --> 00:03:12.308
Henry winced.

64
00:03:12.969 --> 00:03:15.811
Sometimes Maggie could sound rude when she questioned people!

65
00:03:17.152 --> 00:03:18.673
Mr. Collins looked surprised.

66
00:03:18.693 --> 00:03:20.475
"Am I a suspect?

67
00:03:21.275 --> 00:03:22.977
Luckily I have an alibi."

68
00:03:22.997 --> 00:03:24.298
"You do?"

69
00:03:24.638 --> 00:03:26.940
Henry was glad the man didn't seem insulted.

70
00:03:27.976 --> 00:03:29.116
Mr. Collins nodded.

71
00:03:29.136 --> 00:03:30.857
"I've been at Mrs.

72
00:03:30.897 --> 00:03:34.338
Sweet's booth for the past hour or so, learning how to make candy.

73
00:03:35.298 --> 00:03:36.498
She could tell you that too."

74
00:03:36.518 --> 00:03:39.219
"Okay," Henry said.

75
00:03:39.239 --> 00:03:42.200
"Well, we'd better get back to investigating."

76
00:03:43.260 --> 00:03:45.061
The Lemonade Detectives hurried away.

77
00:03:45.081 --> 00:03:48.042
"Are we going to check his alibi?"

78
00:03:48.282 --> 00:03:48.982
Maggie asked.

79
00:03:49.942 --> 00:03:50.782
Henry shrugged.

80
00:03:50.802 --> 00:03:53.623
"I suppose we should, just to be sure.

81
00:03:54.323 --> 00:03:56.004
But I bet he's telling the truth."

82
00:03:57.192 --> 00:03:58.553
"Yeah," Cole agreed.

83
00:03:58.573 --> 00:04:01.815
"His alibi explains why we couldn't find him earlier."

84
00:04:02.835 --> 00:04:04.496
They walked toward the crafts fair.

85
00:04:05.196 --> 00:04:07.558
As they passed the bandstand, Henry spotted Owen.

86
00:04:07.578 --> 00:04:10.039
"Hi," Henry greeted him.

87
00:04:10.059 --> 00:04:11.800
"Have you seen Patrick?"

88
00:04:12.961 --> 00:04:13.781
Owen frowned.

89
00:04:13.801 --> 00:04:17.043
"Not since I saw you guys earlier," he said.

90
00:04:17.063 --> 00:04:20.805
"We were supposed to meet at the crafts fair ten minutes ago.

91
00:04:21.745 --> 00:04:25.027
When he didn't show up, I came here to see if he was at the burger stand.

92
00:04:25.628 --> 00:04:26.228
But he wasn't."

93
00:04:27.252 --> 00:04:30.793
Just then Henry noticed a tall, thin figure moving through the crowd.

94
00:04:30.813 --> 00:04:32.994
"Look," he said.

95
00:04:33.014 --> 00:04:35.254
"It's that strange woman!"

96
00:04:35.274 --> 00:04:37.955
"Quick! We have to catch her!"

97
00:04:38.535 --> 00:04:41.176
Cole took off, with Henry and Maggie right behind him.

98
00:04:42.196 --> 00:04:45.157
The woman was walking quickly toward the museum at the edge of the park.

99
00:04:45.177 --> 00:04:47.017
"Excuse me!"

100
00:04:47.337 --> 00:04:47.998
Henry yelled.

101
00:04:48.018 --> 00:04:49.238
"Wait up!"

102
00:04:50.238 --> 00:04:51.419
The woman glanced back.

103
00:04:52.259 --> 00:04:56.380
When she saw Henry and the others coming, she gasped and dashed toward the museum.

104
00:04:57.480 --> 00:04:59.801
She ran up the steps, disappearing inside.

105
00:04:59.821 --> 00:05:02.283
"Stop!" Maggie yelled.

106
00:05:03.223 --> 00:05:05.484
The Lemonade Detectives ran into the museum.

107
00:05:06.565 --> 00:05:08.266
It was cool and dim inside.

108
00:05:09.266 --> 00:05:14.529
The sound of footsteps echoed off the walls, but Henry couldn't tell which direction they were coming from.

109
00:05:14.549 --> 00:05:16.170
"This way!"

110
00:05:16.430 --> 00:05:17.651
Cole cried, pointing.

111
00:05:18.691 --> 00:05:22.113
Henry turned just in time to see the woman disappear around a corner.

112
00:05:23.274 --> 00:05:26.776
He ran after her and burst into a large room filled with sculptures.

113
00:05:27.912 --> 00:05:28.852
"Where'd she go?"

114
00:05:29.152 --> 00:05:30.033
Maggie exclaimed.

115
00:05:30.053 --> 00:05:32.553
"There!" Henry cried.

116
00:05:34.294 --> 00:05:38.415
The Lemonade Detectives followed the woman through the next room, which was filled with paintings.

117
00:05:39.396 --> 00:05:41.976
Then she escaped into a hallway with lots of doors.

118
00:05:43.837 --> 00:05:45.257
Cole glanced at all the doors.

119
00:05:47.418 --> 00:05:48.338
"Which way did she go?"

120
00:05:48.919 --> 00:05:50.159
he asked breathlessly.

121
00:05:51.219 --> 00:05:53.420
A door leading outside was swinging shut.

122
00:05:54.476 --> 00:05:57.806
Henry hurried over and looked out into the Belltown Arts Day crowd.

123
00:05:59.571 --> 00:06:00.092
He sighed.

124
00:06:00.113 --> 00:06:02.439
"I think we lost her."
